UID:fFVVSepO-bBSM7bNm09zS
SUMMARY:Houston Linux User Group
DTSTAMP:20260703T173428Z
DTSTART:20260716T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested or already invested in the Linux Operating S
	ystem?\nJoin us at the Houston Linux User Group\, one of the oldest user g
	roups involved with the Linux Operating System. We discuss new trends in o
	perating system usage\, software development\, and current technological t
	rends\, as well as provide one-on-one training or class-based instruction.
	 Learn about how to get more out of your computer or how to leverage any o
	f the Linux-based computational platforms.\nAll are welcome to attend\, re
	gardless of whether you’re a seasoned Linux professional intent on network
	ing or a new Linux user struggling with installation or the command line.\
	nThis monthly meeting includes all of the standard Houston Linux User Grou
	p meeting activities\, which include meet-and-greet\, presentations of per
	sonal projects\, multi-meeting classes\, as well as organizational and coo
	rdinating announcements. \nVisit our website at: https://www.houstonlinux.
	org/\nVisit our calendar and the agenda of each week’s meeting at: https:/
	/calendar.google.com/calendar/u/0/embed?src=houstonlinuxusergroup@gmail.co
	m \nJoin us on social media.\nDiscord: https://discord.gg/MPzYfeJz\nReddit
	: https://www.reddit.com/r/houstonlinuxusergroup/\n\nhttps://iondistrict.c
	om/event/houston-linux-user-group-6/\n\nFrom Ion District
URL:https://iondistrict.com/event/houston-linux-user-group-6/
LOCATION:Ion – Conference Room 029 – 030\, 4201 Main St\, Houston\, TX\, 77
	002\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ion-district
CATEGORIES:Ion District
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hmh.org/wp-content
 /uploads/All-the-Horrors-of-War.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://hmh.org/wp-content/uploads/All-the-Horror
 s-of-War.jpg
UID:p3V4cWZ1p0g---_TKjBBD
SUMMARY:Educating Traumatized Teenagers: The Extraordinary Story of a Swedi
	sh International School
DTSTAMP:20260703T173428Z
DTSTART:20260716T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:After World War II\, Sweden absorbed and provided medical treat
	ment for thousands of sick survivors. What to do about those who were teen
	agers\, who had missed years of study on account of the war?  In September
	 1945\, the Swedish government issued an order for schooling to be offered
	 to those under the age of 18. In this presentation\, Dr. Bernice Lerner w
	ill describe the complex process of recruiting wary adolescents\, the chal
	lenges of teaching homeless\, orphaned\, and “environmentally damaged” tee
	nagers\, and instructors’ goals and methods at the most experimental of si
	tes—the “Internat” school her mother attended. \nDr. Bernice Lerner is the
	 author of All the Horrors of War: A Jewish Girl\, a British Doctor\, and 
	the Liberation of Bergen-Belsen\, and other writings on the Holocaust and 
	on virtue ethics. She is the former dean of adult learning at Hebrew Colle
	ge\, former lecturer on the Holocaust at Boston University\, and a senior 
	scholar at Boston University’s Center for Character and Social Responsibil
	ity. \nGerald S. Kaplan Endowed Lecture.\n\nhttps://hmh.org/event/educatin
	g-traumatized-teenagers-the-extraordinary-story-of-a-swedish-international
	-school/\n\nFrom Holocaust Museum Houston
URL:https://hmh.org/event/educating-traumatized-teenagers-the-extraordinary
	-story-of-a-swedish-international-school/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:holocaust-museum-houston
CATEGORIES:Holocaust Museum Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
